{"operations":[{"content":"# Signature limit\n\nA single signature suffices for purchases up to one thousand (1000) EUR only, as stated in the CFO directive of 1 July 2026[[cite:obs-73bc6af41bc0d391468719631983f0077dadac47 \"Until further notice a single signature suffices for purchases up to one thousand (1000) EUR only.\"]].\n\nWhere the CFO directive of 1 July 2026 and the procurement policy differ, the directive applies[[cite:obs-73bc6af41bc0d391468719631983f0077dadac47 \"Until further notice a single signature suffices for purchases up to one thousand (1000) EUR only.\"]].\n\nThe procurement policy states that a single signature suffices for purchases up to two thousand (2000) EUR[[cite:obs-17ee3f5895ceb2da8d2064017cbb1dfafd4638ef \"A single signature suffices for purchases up to two thousand (2000) EUR.\"]].\n","expected_sha256":"8d07a5c6ace44eef23c8280dc7333792f980c8e8ce718a47376785505b32009c","kind":"modify","path":"doc/signature_limit.md"}],"rationale":"Added the single-signature purchase limit from the CFO directive and noted that it overrides the procurement policy, with exact citations for each statement."}